## What to deliver

Build and rig the Boiler up operation by operation until each `parts/<part>.png` matches the
brief, the assembled `scene/` previews show the parts fitting together correctly, and the
rig is complete: a tall riveted brass pressure vessel on short legs straddling a vent, capped
by a tall iron chimney stack, with a bank of pistons down one flank, and a verdigris accent
on the riveted bands sculpted **only** in `#2f7d72` and appearing nowhere else on the model.
**Author the two required animations** as F-curves with the `voxel-anim` animation
subcommands: an **`idle`** (a barely-moving self-playing loop that ticks the vessel and rests
the pistons while the plant stays banked) and a **`boil`** (a hard-working loop that pumps
the pistons down the flank, shudders the vessel, and reads unmistakably as active production
distinct from the idle). The animations and the accent region are the fixed contract —
produce all of them; the parts and joints that realize them are yours. You may add your own
extra parts, joints, or animations on top, but do not drop or contradict the required `idle`
and `boil`. Before you finish, run `voxel-anim render` so it emits the per-part `.glb`
geometry your result is built from — an unrendered part is scored as empty (`voxel-anim
render --component <part>` redraws one part; `voxel-anim render --time <ms> --animation
<name>` renders the model posed at that instant of an animation to check the motion). When
you are satisfied, stop: the recorded per-part logs and `rig.json` are your finished
submission.
